# Find The Needle, Brazilian Portuguese.
#
# An empty msgstr is not a bug: it means the string falls back to its message
# id, which is the English source text. See docs/localization/PLAN.md.
#
# Two plural forms, and zero takes the plural: msgstr[0] is one alone and
# msgstr[1] is everything else, the English rule. gettext's stock pt_BR line
# is (n > 1), which counts zero with one, and a Brazilian reads "0 agulha" on
# the slot card as a typo; "0 agulhas" is how zero is written.
#
# The options row and the picker carry this language as "pt", so a Portuguese
# Windows from either side of the Atlantic lands on it.
#
# To bring this file up to date after the English has moved:
#     python scripts/dev/gen_pot.py --merge pt_BR
msgid ""
msgstr ""
"Project-Id-Version: Find The Needle\n"
"Language: pt_BR\n"
"MIME-Version: 1.0\n"
"Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8\n"
"Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit\n"
"Plural-Forms: nplurals=2; plural=(n != 1);\n"

msgid "SMALL"
msgstr "PEQUENO"

msgid "Designed for weaker computers. A shorter hunt with room to walk around the pile."
msgstr "Feito para computadores mais fracos. Uma busca mais curta, com espaço para andar em volta do monte."

msgid "STANDARD"
msgstr "PADRÃO"

msgid "The yard as it comes. The pile the game was built around, under one steel roof."
msgstr "O pátio do jeito que vem. O jogo foi feito para este monte, debaixo de um telhado de aço."

msgid "BIG"
msgstr "GRANDE"

msgid "Twice the hay and a crown that stands over the wall plates. Bring a belt."
msgstr "O dobro de feno, com o topo passando do alto das paredes. Traga uma esteira."

msgid "HUGE"
msgstr "ENORME"

msgid "Eight storeys of straw. The shed goes out to meet it and the roof still loses. Slow to load."
msgstr "Oito andares de feno. O galpão cresce junto e mesmo assim o telhado não dá conta. Demora para carregar."

msgid "THE MOUNTAIN"
msgstr "A MONTANHA"

msgid "Fifty metres. It does not fit under the roof, it is not supposed to, and you will not finish it. Takes a minute to pour."
msgstr "Cinquenta metros. Não cabe debaixo do telhado, nem era para caber, e você não vai chegar ao fim. Só despejar o feno já leva um minuto."

